--- a/fixture/README.md
+++ b/fixture/README.md
@@ -6,3 +6,17 @@ Activation facts (from `benchmark/results/validation-report-2026-08-30.md`):
 
 - With this plugin attached, dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cold boot immediately fails with `plugin tree failed ... pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)` and exit 1;
 - After migrating per the skill card (`inject: ["llm"]` + `ctx.llm.listProviders()` + removing the dead dependency), activation succeeds; with no API key in the container, a route count of 0 is expected — as long as the calls go through.
+
+## Migration status (dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+The tree now carries the migrated form of the second activation fact, so it is no longer a
+verbatim copy of `/tmp/demo-plugin`:
+
+- `index.js` injects the `llm` domain service and reads the host provider directory with
+  `ctx.llm.listProviders()`; the removed `apiProxy` facade is not referenced anywhere;
+- `package.json` no longer declares the dead `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy` dependency;
+- `cordis.patch.yml` is unchanged: the bundle still mounts the `upgrade-demo` row.
+
+Verified against the pinned `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` host with the model route pointed at a dead
+port: the tree activates, `ctx.llm.listProviders()` returns `[]` without a credential, and
+the boot reaches the model call (`dsh: TRANSPORT: ...`).
